codex
I found a regression in the cost module’s dataclass binding: it moves a standard-library-generated `__repr__` wrapper into globals that lack `_thread`, so representing returned records can raise `NameError`. The restore also rejects a fresh destination whose parent does not yet exist, including the documented new-machine recovery case.

